WEBVTT

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.370
It sure seems quiet now.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.940
That's because the Royal Guard left for the capital.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:17.580
It may be calm here, but Endora is about to get crazy.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.720
Very true...

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.690
The chaos and bloodshed has already begun.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:27.120
With Delzaine dead, the situation has changed.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.090
In any case, we'll need to group up and work together with the Ignauts.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.260
We'll need a report on each of the regions.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.700
Yes, sir.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:42.740
The time has come to prove our worth...

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.470
Frustrating, isn't it?

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:48.580
We can't leave until they've finished investigating Babel.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:52.780
Yeah, but we can be ready to leave the moment they're done.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.920
By the way, is he still moping about?

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.820
Yes, a bit...

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.310
That's understandable.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:17.910
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:27.910
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:38.290
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:48.290
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:58.470
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.990
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:18.990
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:29.670
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.430
Pascal, I see no problems here.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.490
It's functioning as expected.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:48.160
All's well over here too.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:52.500
Babel operated exactly according to design.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:58.270
But still there's no evidence that Zoozian called Ibelda was actually sent to the surface.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:03.750
Which means unless we investigate from the surface itself, we won't know what happened.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.450
That's true...

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.420
What could have possibly gone wrong on the surface?

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.960
I can't say for sure without seeing for myself, but...

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:18.050
I'd guess the path was somehow blocked on the surface.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:22.460
We keep running into problem after problem!

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:26.200
But that's what makes research and science so great!

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.440
It's like we've got two Pascal's now...

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:31.710
Hello, Alicia.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.110
I brought some food. Why not take a break?

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.550
Thanks. Don't mind if I do.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.980
Joseph! Time to eat!

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:42.320
Joseph!

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:47.090
Every answer brings us one step further down the path of truth!

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.920
--Is he even listening?
--I've done it!

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:53.830
"14: Resume"

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:59.270
Isn't it a good thing if the path to the surface is blocked?

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:04.070
I mean, weren't you opposed to joining Endora and the surface?

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.170
And I still am even now.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.850
But Shun still needs to get back to the surface.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.280
Yeah...

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:23.590
With King Delzaine gone, there are so many things that we'll never know...

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:26.860
What was the king trying to accomplish...

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:28.600
Hey, Pascal.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.330
What is it?

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:31.630
Emilio's feeling down, right?

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.140
Yeah...

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:36.270
Is there anything I can do for him?

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:38.270
I wonder the same.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:41.280
That boy is lost in his own thoughts.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:44.370
I'd like to help him as much as you, but...

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.150
Hey!

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:49.390
Shun? What's up?

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:53.520
Well, I was wondering how the investigation was going.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.460
Oh, man...

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:03.130
We lack both the time and resources to investigate any further.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:07.540
I'm very sorry about not being able to return you to the surface.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:13.340
Don't gimme that. It's not like this means I'll never get back.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.810
You and that guy... Joseph, right?

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:20.250
I'm sure you two will figure out how to make Babel work eventually.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:25.090
Even if you don't, I'll just find another way to get home.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.160
Another way?

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.890
But you know...

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:34.060
Before any of that, there's someone we've got to cheer up.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.830
I can't let him stay depressed forever.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:42.430
Emilio sure has some good friends.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.880
It's over capacity!

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.510
Curse this advanced prehistoric technology!

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:52.510
Hot! Hot!

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:56.390
I'll just have to compensate for the pressure using a larger volume...

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:57.750
How's that? Argh!

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:03.460
Emilio might just need a distraction to take his mind off things...

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.960
A distraction?

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.360
I've got it.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.430
We're counting on you.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:09.860
Yes, sir.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:17.710
Demetrio. What was that about?

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:21.480
Just keeping in touch with our comrades.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:25.880
Now that Delzaine has died, some regions are falling into disarray.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.380
Demetrio.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.280
What are your plans now?

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.990
Plans?

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:36.620
I... With Delzaine dead,
I lost my one and only purpose.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.460
Isn't it the same for you?

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:44.070
The king is dead. Your revolution is over.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.930
So what do you plan to do now?

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:48.770
It's not over just because he's dead.

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:50.810
Our real purpose begins now.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:51.770
Huh?

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:55.610
The disorder in this country will only worsen from here.

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:57.750
Turmoil and unrest will spread.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:02.850
Regional lords will brawl and feud to expand their own greed and lands.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:07.260
And until it all passes over, the Ignauts will have a job to do.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:13.000
We'll be on our way as soon as they're done investigating Babel.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:16.690
Do you plan on staying here and moping forever?

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:30.150
Emilio? What were you and Demetrio talking about?

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:32.180
That's none of your business.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.680
What do you want?

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:38.950
I'm sick of sitting around.
Thought I'd get in a little training.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.230
Want to spar together?

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.720
Hurry up and get out your Warp Relic.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.400
Practice by yourself.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.670
I don't feel like it right now.

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:54.400
What's your problem? I even asked nicely...

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:57.240
You can't even go back to the surface now.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.910
Why are you still acting so positive?

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:02.180
You happy-go-lucky moron.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:04.880
Of course I'm not happy about it.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.650
But you know...

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:10.720
Being depressed about it isn't going to help anything.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:13.920
I'm not useless like you.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.980
Does that make you mad, prince?

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:48.090
Not bad...

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:52.590
If you think that's impressive, you must not be very good.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.030
Don't underestimate me!

00:08:55.200 --> 00:09:00.100
Those kids... Though maybe
I'm the one who's a child.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:09.410
First we'll have to head to nearby towns and secure rations and supplies.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:10.810
After that...

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.890
What do you want?

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:20.720
Mischa...

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:23.660
I'm thinking to leave the Ignauts.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.260
But why?!

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:28.800
Because... I'm a traitor.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:32.830
None of you will feel the same with me around.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.410
Goodbye...

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:47.320
Huh?

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.080
What's the matter?

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:52.120
The island Zoozians are seeking help.

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:54.090
What happened?

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:57.490
The island was surrounded by armed ships.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:02.620
But why? That island has always been left alone...

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.330
Your island now belongs to me!

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:42.640
You no longer have to suffer your pitiful lives.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:47.340
When you labor as slaves of mine,
I will guarantee your safety.

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:58.050
Did you hear? The king passed away in Babylon!

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:01.590
Now lords from all over are raiding villages and towns.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.590
What a mess this has become...

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:05.830
Even Prince Emilio has gone missing.

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:08.230
This country is falling apart!

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:12.100
Gimme everything you've got!

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.100
Hand it over! Quick!

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:17.610
Y-You'll never get away with this.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.010
Give it back!

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:20.410
Shut up!

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:23.850
This is for not cooperating!

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.920
With the king dead, the army and government is in shambles!

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.410
There's no one around to stop us!

00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:39.530
There's nothing holding this country together anymore.

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:44.230
And without the king, there's nothing to stop people from invading the Zoozian island.

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:46.440
I'm afraid you're right.

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:50.030
Our work as a revolutionary army is over.

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:58.610
Now we must quell the riots before they get any worse.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:06.320
In the Ignauts, no one will stop you from coming or leaving.

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:08.260
Louise...

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.950
The choice is yours whether to stay or go.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:18.230
There is still something I must do...

00:12:18.230 --> 00:12:19.840
What?

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.640
What is it then?

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:26.640
I... I wish to stay and support the Ignauts.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.340
Louise...

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:31.950
You said you were leaving.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:35.920
I thought I had to in order to pay for my sin.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:42.790
But if the Ignauts' work isn't yet over,
I'll make up for what I did through service.

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:45.360
Even though you betrayed us...

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:47.100
I did...

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:50.470
That's why I don't expect you to trust me.

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:53.140
It's fine if you don't think of me as a comrade.

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:57.100
But I'll do whatever
I can to help, comrade or not.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.480
What do you think, Demetrio?

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.680
Do you even have to ask?

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:09.520
Louise, there's not a time in my life I haven't trusted you.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:10.650
But...

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:15.190
The Louise that betrayed us isn't her real self.

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:21.630
And given her situation, she may be able to see what we cannot.

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.670
Eljuia...

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:25.230
You pushover...

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:28.240
I knew Demetrio would do this...

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:31.870
You think you know everything about Demetrio.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:32.910
I hate it...

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.640
I've known him longer than you.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:40.580
I'll keep an eye on Louise.
If she's up to something, I'll know it.

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:41.880
I'll watch her, too.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.520
You're a copycat.

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:44.490
I am not.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:44.920
You are!

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:45.650
Am not.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:47.050
You are!

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:50.590
Thank you...

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:54.160
Louise...

00:13:57.670 --> 00:14:02.940
You don't have to kill your heart like you did before.

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:07.400
Just do what your heart tells you is right.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.940
What the hell am I doing?

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:40.040
I always just play right into his hands...

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.570
What's even the point of all this?!

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.750
Just leave me alone already!

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:49.120
It shouldn't even matter to you!

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:50.950
Of course it matters!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:54.820
We're on a journey together and you're stuck in a rut!

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:56.490
I can't just leave you behind!

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.120
I see...

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:02.900
Here I come!

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:15.340
Ow...

00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:17.250
It's my win.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:19.180
Dammit!

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.610
Here.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.090
I didn't realize.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:27.520
What? What are you on about?

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:33.160
You were trying to cheer me up, weren't you?

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:35.260
That's not entirely true.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:40.500
Would you quit always grumbling and throwing a fit?

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.800
Stop hanging onto the past all the time.

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.010
What?

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:46.170
I'm saying you should think positive.

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:47.180
You...

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:51.310
Before Delzaine, all you thought about was revenge.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:53.780
Now all you talk about is regret.

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:57.380
You're way too obsessed with the past, Emilio.

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:03.020
You just love being depressed.
You're Prince Gloomy.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:04.330
Prince Gloomy?!

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:10.000
You are though, aren't you?
Always sad and never smiling.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.030
You're right.

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:14.400
Huh? No, sorry. I said too much...

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:18.310
You're supposed to snap back at me like you always do.

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:19.710
This just makes it weird.

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:22.340
No... What you said is true.

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:24.650
I'm too obsessed with the past.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.250
What? You admit it?

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.980
But...

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:31.750
That's because I don't know what to do.

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.380
How am I supposed to live now?

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:37.360
Just move towards the future.

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:40.730
Just do what you can this moment in time.

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:43.500
That's what everyone else is doing.

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:45.590
Do what you can...

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:56.280
I see... I've got it, Shun.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.710
I...

00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:59.780
Hmm?

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:03.720
If we meet up with Gradido, we'll pass through cities here...

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:05.250
...and right here.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:09.220
But both are already being invaded by the local lords.

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:10.860
Demetrio.

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.790
Here you all are.

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:15.560
Yeah. What is it?

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:17.690
I have a favor to ask.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:23.870
It's good to see you perked up a bit.

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:26.070
What? Let's hear it.

00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:28.910
I want to join the Ignauts.

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:36.480
What makes you say that, all of a sudden?

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:41.460
On the way here to Babylon,
I've seen a lot since leaving the capital.

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:46.090
The poverty of the people...
Their unfair treatment...

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:49.760
Those forced into circumstances brought by this injustice...

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:55.170
I want to do something for these suffering people.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.170
But I am powerless...

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:59.640
There's nothing I can do on my own.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.770
So please, I'm begging you.

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:07.350
What are you talking about?

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:09.820
You've been helping us for some time now.

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:13.080
We already consider you as one of us.

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:15.520
Thank you.

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:16.960
All right!

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:21.800
If Emilio is joining, then I've gotta, too!

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:23.870
We don't really need you.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:25.930
What? Why not?!

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:28.870
Don't you know how much
I contributed on this journey?

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:29.870
You contributed?

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:31.640
I sure did!

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:34.780
Mischa! It was before you joined so you don't know!

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:36.310
Am I supposed to care?

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:38.180
--What a lively bunch.
--You really tick me off...

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:43.990
Yes, and the tougher the journey, the greater the need for a positive light.

00:18:43.990 --> 00:18:49.560
Anyways, until I can find a way back home,
I'll be helping you guys out.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:53.500
We may find a hint for that in the capital.

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:56.330
Pascal! What do you mean, the capital?

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:59.800
We've pretty much wrapped up investigating Babel from here.

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:05.310
And we believe the problem somehow originates from the surface.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:10.210
It's as if a lock prevents the path from opening on the other side.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:11.650
I see...

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:13.550
But isn't that weird?

00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:18.420
It's the surface. They don't know about Endora up there, do they?

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:20.260
As far as I know.

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.820
True...

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:28.560
Though we don't know if the lock is human-made or simply incidental.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:33.430
We can't determine the cause at this point in time.

00:19:33.430 --> 00:19:34.100
Shun.

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.500
Hmm?

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:42.910
Right now, our options are to investigate Babel again and research some way to unlock the path...

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:46.280
...or discover a way for you to return without Babel.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:52.920
Either way requires us to return to the
Royal Laboratory and do additional research.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:55.220
So our course of action is clear.

00:19:55.220 --> 00:20:01.860
We return towards the capital bringing order back to the regions we pass through.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.650
All right!

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:23.080
Come on, let's do this!

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:25.140
Why is Shun taking the lead?

00:20:26.150 --> 00:20:28.650
I just felt like it, okay?!

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:38.130
Emilio?

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:41.900
Something happen? You seem much better now.

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:46.010
Maybe...

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:04.930
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:13.800
<i>I've walked very far, so far</i>

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:23.300
<i>And I'll walk even farther from here</i>

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:46.070
<i>I don't wish for everything to stay the same</i>

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:56.070
<i>Because change is what got me to where I am</i>

00:21:56.710 --> 00:22:05.250
<i>We've walked very far, so far</i>

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:13.860
<i>We'll go farther than anyone's gone before</i>

00:22:13.860 --> 00:22:22.400
<i>Each of us can change the world</i>

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:31.570
<i>That's why I smile at you</i>
